"The prognosis is influenced by several documented factors. The surgical findings included a pT3a stage with extraprostatic extension and positive surgical margins, which are adverse prognostic indicators. Conversely, the seminal vesicles were not invaded, and lymphovascular invasion was absent. The absence of documented nodal sampling widens the uncertainty regarding regional disease control. The discrepancy between the preoperative PSA of 7.6 and the surgical pathology details is noted, though the biopsy report lacks specific Gleason pattern and ISUP grading. Missing information, particularly postoperative PSA and its trajectory, significantly limits the ability to refine this assessment. A postoperative PSA measurement and subsequent trend would be crucial in revising the prognosis. The current uncertainty is reflected in the heuristic sensitivity range for recurrence timing. The fixed estimated horizon is 43.67 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 26.20–61.14 months; its coverage has not been validated."
